<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">23 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 23 August, from 406 to 1989.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">406 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,620 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Stilicho executes the Gothic leader Radagaisus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Having trapped Radagaisus's invading army near Faesulae, the Roman general Stilicho had the Gothic king executed. Italy was saved for now, but Rome's frontiers were under mounting pressure.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/london" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/london.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1305 CE <span class="tih-ago">721 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William Wallace is executed in London</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Betrayed and captured near Glasgow, William Wallace was hanged, drawn and quartered at Smithfield. The victor of Stirling Bridge became an enduring symbol of Scottish independence.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1572 CE <span class="tih-ago">454 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">French court resolves to kill the Huguenot leaders</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the eve of St Bartholomew's Day, Charles IX and his council agreed to eliminate the Protestant leaders gathered in Paris. The killings began before dawn and spread across France.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1939 CE <span class="tih-ago">87 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nazi Germany and the Soviet Union sign a non-aggression pact</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Ribbentrop and Molotov signed a pact in Moscow whose secret protocol divided eastern Europe into spheres of influence. It cleared the way for Germany's invasion of Poland a week later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1989 CE <span class="tih-ago">37 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Two million people form the Baltic Way human chain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Some two million people joined hands across Estonia, Latvia and Lithuania on the 50th anniversary of the Nazi-Soviet Pact. The 675 km chain demanded independence, regained in 1990-91.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a></div></div></li></ol>
